<section class="hero compact">
    <p class="eyebrow">EMERALD / REPOSITORIES</p>
    <h1>portsync</h1>

    <p class="lead">Synchronize one or more local ports repositories from their configured remotes.</p>
    <div class="command-line"># portsync [options]</div>
</section>

<section class="doc">
    <h2 id="help">
        <code>portsync help</code>
    </h2>

    <pre><code>Usage:
    portsync &lt;options&gt;

Options:
    -p, --prune	          prune local git repository
    -r, --reset	          reset git repositories
    -s, --source &lt;repos&gt;  sync specific repos only (space-separated)
    -h, --help	          show this help message

Examples:
    portsync                 sync all repos
    portsync --source main   sync only 'main'
    portsync -s main custom  sync 'main' and 'custom'
    portsync -r -s main      reset and sync only 'main' </code></pre>

    <h2 id="usage">Usage</h2>

    <pre><code>portsync --help
portsync
portsync -s core</code></pre>

    <p>
        <code>emerald sync</code> is the high-level entrypoint and invokes the
        synchronization phase. Use <code>portsync</code> directly when
        diagnosing repository checkouts or scripting a lower-level refresh.
    </p>
</section>
